        "original_id": "c769770e-fc6f-5d17-b012-16158245ea9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Louise, Le roi malgré lui, Julien\n- People: Gustave Charpentier, Saint-Pol-Roux, Emmanuel Chabrier, Emile de Najac, Paul Burani\n- Concepts: opera, opéra-comique, libretto, sequel\n\nFacts:\n- In 1887, Emmanuel Chabrier's Le roi malgré lui was presented as an opéra-comique in three acts with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\n- In 1900, Gustave Charpentier's Louise was an opera described as a \"roman musical\" in four acts with an original French libretto by the composer.\n- Saint-Pol-Roux, a symbolist poet who inspired the surrealists, contributed to the libretto of Louise.\n- Julien is a sequel to Gustave Charpentier's Louise and depicts the artistic aspirations of Louise's suitor Julien.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
